---
import '@fontsource-variable/roboto-serif';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactForm from '../components/ContactForm.astro';
import WhoFor from '../components/WhoFor.astro';
import { rates, gbp, offerDays } from '../data/rates';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="AI Product Audit | Saielle DaSilva"
  description={`A fixed-price AI product audit from Saielle DaSilva, fractional CPO for AI products. In ${offerDays.aiAudit} days across one week, every AI feature shipped or planned gets a keep, change or stop call, agreed with the leadership team. ${gbp(rates.aiAudit)}.`}
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Fixed scope · {offerDays.aiAudit} days · {gbp(rates.aiAudit)}</p>
      <h1>Know which AI work to keep, change or stop. In one week.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Saielle DaSilva reviews every AI feature you have shipped or planned,
        and your leadership team leaves agreeing what to fund next and what to
        stop.
      </p>
    </header>

    <WhoFor
      fit={[
        'Leadership teams with several AI pilots or features and no shared view of which ones matter.',
        'Companies about to commit budget to AI work and wanting an outside read first.',
        'CEOs and CTOs who need a straight answer they can take to the board.',
      ]}
      notFit={[
        'You already know what to build and need it built. Start with forward-deployed work.',
        'You need someone to lead product week to week. Start with fractional leadership.',
      ]}
    />

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Sound familiar?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Several AI pilots are running, and nobody can say which one the business depends on.</li>
        <li>The demo looks good. Nobody can say what a user is supposed to do with the output.</li>
        <li>The board asks about AI every quarter, and the answer changes every quarter.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What Saielle looks at</h2>
      <p>Every AI feature, shipped or planned, against the same questions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The decision.</strong> What does a user do differently because of the output?</li>
        <li><strong>The value.</strong> Is the thing it automates the expensive part of the job?</li>
        <li><strong>The data.</strong> Has the model met real data, including the messy half?</li>
        <li><strong>The risk.</strong> What happens when it is confidently wrong, and who is accountable?</li>
        <li><strong>The cost.</strong> What each answer costs to run, and whether that holds at scale.</li>
        <li><strong>The evidence.</strong> Can you tell whether it is working, and from what?</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What you leave with</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A ranked list of your AI work: keep, change or stop, with the reason for each.</li>
        <li>The one or two bets worth funding next, and the evidence that would prove them.</li>
        <li>The failure modes written down, before a customer finds them.</li>
        <li>A leadership team that agrees, because it made the calls together in the readout.</li>
        <li>A plain recommendation on what happens next, including when the answer is nothing.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How the week runs</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Day one.</strong> Saielle reviews the product, the data and the AI plans with the people who own them.</li>
        <li><strong>Day two.</strong> A half-day readout workshop where your leadership team makes the keep, change and stop calls, then the written plan.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why Saielle DaSilva</h2>
      <p>
        At Sainsbury's, Saielle DaSilva ran product for AI, data platforms and
        machine learning, and took production AI from a handful of experiments
        to a platform serving over 100 million customers. She was on the
        founding team at <a href="/case-studies/cazoo/">Cazoo</a>, through to a
        $7B IPO.
      </p>

      <h2>What it costs</h2>
      <p>
        {gbp(rates.aiAudit)}, fixed. The fee is credited against a
        <a href="/fractional/">fractional engagement</a> that starts within
        30 days.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="contact-form-section" aria-label="Get in touch">
      <div class="contact-card">
        <h2>Book an audit.</h2>
        <ContactForm source="ai-product-audit" selected="strategic-direction" booking />
      </div>
      <p class="faq-link">
        Questions first? <a href="/faq/">Read the FAQ.</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
